<title>BELGIUM: TABLE - Gevaert H1 cons net up 23.8 pct.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Gevaert H1 cons net up 23.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1997</p>
<p>(in millions of Belgian francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Profit per share (francs)	 181	     vs    146</p>
<p>    Gross dividend (francs/share)   150	     vs    n/a</p>
<p>    Cons net profit		  4,667		vs 3,769</p>
<p>    Current income		   1,446		vs 1,538</p>
<p>    Net income cap transactions* 3,244		vs 2,246</p>
<p>NOTE - Holding company Gevaert said the period was marked by sustained low interest rates and higher stock prices at home and abroad. It gave no forecast for the full year.</p>
<p>* Gevaert said it sold a relatively large proportion of its holding in Bayer, the remainder of its holding in Electrabel, its holding in Hibernia of the U.S., and some of its shares in KNP BT.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
